    "metadata": {
      "designIntent": "CARD 016b — The Same Podium. Not a corruption node, a mirror. The player returns to the exact podium of their first speech and is asked, plainly, whether they still mean the thing they said there. LEFT costs Standing to reaffirm (honoring a promise under pressure is now expensive); RIGHT is the soft, popular betrayal — no scandal, no obligation, just quietly saying the newer thing. The witness fires on RIGHT with the player's own first line. Appears only for players holding at least one promise who have already set at least one precedent; the pure cynic never sees this podium."
    }
